<title>USA: Navy exercises option on Hughes missiles.</title>
<headline>Navy exercises option on Hughes missiles.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hughes Electronics Corp's missile unit said Friday the U.S. Naval Air Systems Command has exercised its option to procure 120 fiscal 1997 Tomahawk Cruise Missiles under its fiscal 1994-98 production contract.</p>
<p>The option is valued at approximately $65 million.</p>
<p>The company said the missiles will be produced at the Hughes facility in Tucson, and at the company's Sycamore Canyon facility near Poway, Calif. They are scheduled to be delivered to the Navy by September 1999.</p>
<p>Hughes is a unit of General Motors Corp.</p>
</text>
